course: dictionary
lesson: 16169
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word wrench can be a noun or a verb, and it has several meanings. Read the words around it to find out which one is meant. «She picked up the wrench and turned the bolt.» You turn bolts with a wrench, so here it is a tool.
explain: «He had to wrench the stuck door open.» Here wrench is an action. The clues are stuck and open: you pull or twist hard to make the door move. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Leaving the seaside was a wrench.» This wrench is a feeling, not a tool or an action. Leaving was painful and sad, so a wrench here means a sad feeling when you must say goodbye. In The Wind in the Willows, leaving the river is a wrench for Mole and Rat, too.
fact: Wrench can be a noun (a tool, or a sad feeling) or a verb (to pull or twist something suddenly and hard).
fact: «Wrench» as a tool means a metal tool for gripping and turning nuts and bolts. In the UK this is usually called a spanner.
fact: «Wrench» as a verb means to pull or twist something suddenly and hard, as in «wrench the door open».
fact: To wrench a joint means to injure it by twisting it, as in «I wrenched my ankle». If this happens, rest it, put ice on it, raise it, and tell an adult.
fact: A wrench can also be a sad feeling when you have to leave someone or something.
exercise: «The mechanic used a wrench to loosen the bolt.» What is a wrench in this sentence? | A loud noise | A sad feeling | *A metal tool for turning nuts and bolts | A kind of bird
exercise: «Sam had to wrench the lid off the jar.» What does wrench mean here? | To sleep late | To paint a picture | To sing softly | *To pull or twist something suddenly and hard
exercise: «Saying goodbye to her best friend was a wrench.» What does wrench mean in this sentence? | *A sad feeling when you have to leave someone | A tool for fixing bikes | A happy feeling at a surprise party | A quick run around the field
test: «Ben wrenched his ankle when he fell off the wall.» What does wrenched mean here? | Painted it bright blue | *Twisted a joint and hurt it | Climbed higher | Laughed loudly
test: In the UK, what is another name for a wrench? | Spoon | Brush | *Spanner | Hammer
exam: Which sentence uses wrench to mean a sad feeling? | «The bolts were rusty.» | *«Moving house was a wrench, and she said goodbye to her friends.» | «The wrench was lying on the workbench.» | «He gave the gate a wrench.»
